-- GAME ----------------------------------------------------------------------
  Title       Lunar Jetman
  Publisher   Ultimate, 1983
  Version     1.0

-- YOU NEED ------------------------------------------------------------------
  Your own copy of the original game, saved beside this patch:

  File        Lunar Jetman (1983)(Ultimate Play The Game).z80
  MD5         4fd3f151dcf12216cb23618687da04d5

  The patch carries none of the game's code. It only works with that exact
  dump, under that name or any other: anything else is refused, with a
  message naming the file it wants.

-- WHAT IT DOES --------------------------------------------------------------
  Moving figures become Next hardware sprites, so they keep their own colours
  and no longer take on the scenery's (colour clash). Game logic is unchanged.

  Colours     Default (the game's own) plus: Enhanced, chosen on the menu, off
              by default.
  Enhanced    Jetman in the suit of the Spec256 Jetpac; every alien family
              painted by its parts in its own colours; the moon rover in blue
              and cyan with dark grey tyres and light grey spokes. No white
              outlines or edges. Source: Jetman's Enhanced suit from an older
              Spec256 Jetpac conversion, painter not established.

  Note        The patch writes the whole alt ROM image (Sinclair's ROM plus
              its hooks), so the ROM's own interrupt code can never run the
              hooks. Known issues: none found in testing. Missing: pace not
              measured against the original; the cheats are unplayed by a
              person; not reached in testing: the alien base, the missile's
              flight, the rover carrying items and later levels; hardware
              untested.

-- MENU ----------------------------------------------------------------------
   1  Infinite lives
   2  Infinite fuel
   3  No enemies

  Cheats come from the archive's POKEs for this release.

