-- TESTING -------------------------------------------------------------------
  Tested      Played by Jon Attree in JNext through the real loader,
              2026-11-04

  Replay      IDENTICAL on 3 recordings from the title, 22,090 frames, default
              and Enhanced, on the whole alt ROM build (2026-11-04: alt ROM
              image is Sinclair's 48K ROM plus the hooks, 0x0000-0x3FFF all
              written by the build): at every hook call (h_new 30,374, h_tnew
              19,761, h_clr 105,103, h_eo 271, h_teo 4, h_cls 44, h_msg 4)
              original and patched code run from the same state to the same
              point, registers and 48K memory compared (dead stack aside),
              slot 4 restored, the patched ROM modelled as the Next fills it
              (NextZXOS's ROM3 first, then the build's writes); at all 21,398
              IM 1 interrupts the alt ROM image's handler run against the
              original's, IDENTICAL, no hook code reached; at 11,971
              interrupts outside the plot code each object's sprite ink equals
              the pixels its own XOR stores put on the original screen (35,595
              object checks), palette offset equal to the object's colour at
              every draw, setup palette checked entry by entry; 10 of 10
              negatives detected on the default and 7 of 7 on Enhanced, the
              new one in both the previous build's image (hooks only over
              ROM3): hook code ran from the IM 1 handler at every interrupt;
              Enhanced tiles checked against their default tiles, silhouette
              for silhouette; the verified start is the stepped s0 state, and
              the shipped build starts at the file's own decrypter, proven in
              the simulator to reach the same memory at 0x8000 apart from 16
              bytes of ROM keyboard and frame variables and dead stack

  Emulator    JNext 1.1.104 headless, whole alt ROM build (2026-11-04): menu,
              play, the rover, aliens and bombs, default and Enhanced, frames
              viewed; the alt ROM image dumped in JNext equals the modelled
              Sinclair-plus-hooks image; with NextZXOS's DivMMC 0x0038 trap
              removed IM 1 ran Sinclair's handler 4,470 times and play ran to
              game over and the Hall of Fame; earlier, on the previous build:
              the tape's loading picture held then the game, walking pace
              equal to the plain build, real loader from the Browser, MD5
              exact

  Coverage    random play with infinite lives on 3 recordings: walking,
              flying, firing, aliens of the first levels, bombs, the rover
              moving and destroyed, the missile warning, game over and the
              Hall of Fame; not reached: the alien base, the missile's flight
              and destruction, bombing the base, the rover carrying items,
              later levels; cheats from the archive's POKEs for this release
              (its "Infinite Lives (corrected)" bytes, and fuel and no-enemies
              written for the rotated code), lives, fuel and no enemies held
              in the simulator on the original code, unplayed by a person;
              whole alt ROM image from 2026-11-04: the previous build differs
              only in the alt ROM fill (stub) and the image's low half

  Hardware    none

  Nothing here claims a result on real hardware unless the line above says so.

-- HOW TO USE ----------------------------------------------------------------
  Put this .nxc and the game file in the same folder on the Next's card and
  choose the .nxc in the Browser. See README.txt.
